{"id":"word:hebrew:H995","type":"word","title":"בִּין","subtitle":"H995 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to separate mentally (or distinguish ), i.e.(generally) understand","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בִּין (H995) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 171 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בִּין (bîyn) means to separate mentally (or distinguish ), i.e.(generally) understand First listed occurrence: 1Chr 15 22."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בִּין","transliteration":"bîyn","pronunciation":"bene","strong":"H995","lemmaId":"hebrew:H995","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["יָבִ֥ין","נָ֭בוֹן","מֵבִ֖ין","מֵבִ֥ין","יָבִ֖ינוּ"],"morphs":[["HVqi3ms",19],["HVhrmsa",15],["HVqi3mp",10],["HVNrmsa",9],["HVri1cs",6],["HVhv2ms/Sp1cs",6],["HVhc",5],["HR/Vhc",4],["HVqi1cs",4],["HVqi2ms",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"to separate mentally (or distinguish ), i.e.(generally) understand","usage":"attend, consider, be cunning, diligently, direct, discern, eloquent, feel, inform, instruct, have intelligence, know, look well to, mark, perceive, be prudent, regard, (can) skill(-full), teach, think, (cause, make to, get, give, have) understand(-ing), view, (deal) wise(-ly, man).","full":"H995. bin בִּין verb discern (Nö ZMG 1883, 592 f. ; Arabic become separated, be distinct , IV. speak perspicuously ; Ethiopic 1. 2 consider, perceive , Aramaic make to understand , compare Sabean בין ( the ) wise , as epithet, Mordt ZMG 1876, 37 ) — Qal Perfect בִּין Dan 10:1 ; בַּנְתָּה Psa 139:2 ; בִּינֹתִי Dan 9:2 ; Imperfect יָבִין Psa 19:13 25t. וְיָבֵן Jer 9:11 2 t., וַיָּבֶן 1Sam 3:8 2 t.; אָבִינָה Psa 73:17 4 t.; יָבִינוּ Prov 28:5 12 t.; Imperative בִּין Dan 9:23 ; בִּינָה Psa 5:2 ; בִּינוּ Deut 32:7 2 t.; Infinitive absolute בִּין Prov 23:1 ; Participle בָּנִים Jer 49:7 ; &#8212; 1 perceive (with the senses); — a. eyes , accusative Prov 7:7 , with לְ Job 9:11 ; 14:21 ; 23:8 ; Prov 14:15 . b. ears , accusative Prov 29:19 , with לְ Job 13:1 . c. touch , accusative Psa 58:10 . d . taste , acc. Job 6:30 . 2 understand, know (with mind): — a. absolute Job 18:2 ; 38:20 ; 42:3 ; Psalm 49:21; Psa 82:5 ; Prov 24:12 ; Isa 6:9-10 , 44:18 ; Dan 12:10 ; Hosea 4:14 ; Hosea 14:10; אבין ולא שׁמעתי I heard but I could not understand Dan 12:8 . b. accusative Job 15:9 ; 23:5 ; 36:29 ; Prov 2:5 , 9 ; 20:24 ; 28:5 ; Psa 19:13 ; 92:7 ; Jer 9:11 ; משׁפט יבין Job 32:9 ; Prov 28:5 ; דעת יבין 29:7 . c. with כִּי 1Sam 3:8 ; 2Sam 12:19 ; Isa 43:10 . d. with infinitive & לָדָֽעַת יבין לְ, Isa 32:4 3 observe, mark, give heed to, distinguish, consider (with attention): — a. accusative Deut 32:7 ; Psa 5:2 ; 50:22 ; 94:7 ; 94:8 ; Prov 23:1 ; 21:29 (Qr) Dan 9:2 ; 10:1 . b. with לְ , Psa 73:17 ; 139:2 ; Deut 32:29 . c. with בְּ , Ezra 8:15 ; Neh 13:7 ; Dan 9:23 . d. with אל , Psa 28:5 . e. with עַל , Dan 11:30 , 37 . 4 have discernment, insight, understanding Jer 49:7 . Niph`al נְבֻנוֺתִי Isa 10:12 ; Participle נָבוֺן Gen 41:33 15 t.; plural נְבוֺנִים Jer 4:22 , elsewhere נְבֹנִים Deut 1:13 ; Isa 5:22 (Baer) Eccl 9:11 ; נְבֹנָיו Isa 29:14 ; be intelligent, discreet, discerning, have understanding 1Sam 16:18 ; Prov 1:5 ; 10:13 ; 14:6 ; 16:21 ; 17:28 ; 19:25 ; Eccl 9:11 ; Isa 3:3 ; 5:21 ; 10:13 ; 29:14 ; Jer 4:22 ; Hosea 14:10; נָבוֺן לֵב intelligent mind Prov 14:33 ; 15:14 ; 18:15 ; וְחָכָם נָבוֺן Gen 41:33 , 39 ; ונבון חכם Deut 4:6 ; 1Kin 3:12 ; ונבנים חכמים Deut 1:13 . Po . יְבוֺנְַנֵהוּ he attentively considereth him Deut 32:10 . Hiph`il Perfect הֵבִין Job 28:33 5 t.; Imperfect יָבִין Isa 28:9 4 t.; וַיָּבֶן 2Chr 11:23 ; Dan 9:22 ; Infinitive הָבִין Psa 32:9 9 t.; Imperative הָבֵן Dan 8:16 12 t.; Participle מֵבִין Prov 28:7 26 t.; — 1 understand: — a. absolute Isa 29:16 ; 40:21 ; 56:11 ; 1Kin 3:11 ; Psa 32:9 ; Dan 8:17 ; 10:12 . b. accusative 1Chr 28:9 ; Job 28:23 ; Prov 1:2 , 6 ; 8:5 ; 14:8 ; Isa 28:19 ; Dan 8:23 ; Micah 4:12 ; מֵבִין one with understanding Prov 8:9 ; 17:10 , 24 ; 28:2 , 7 , 11 ; מַדָּע מְבִינֵי Dan 1:4 ; able to understand (i.e. old enough) Neh 8:3 ; 10:29 , compare 8:2 (followed by לִשׁמֹעַ ). 2 give heed to, attend to, observe, discern , absolute Isa 57:1 ; 2Chr 11:23 ; Dan 8:5 ; with בְּ Neh 8:12 ; Dan 9:23 ; 10:11 ; בְּ מֵבִין skilled in 2Chr 26:5 ; 34:12 ; with אֶל Psa 33:15 ; לרע טוב בין 1Kin 3:9 . 3 give understanding make understand, teach: — a. absolute Dan 8:27 ; 9:22 . b. with accusative of person Psa 119:34 ; 119:73 ; 119:125 ; 119:130 ; 119:144 ; 119:169 ; Job 32:8 ; Neh 8:7 , 9 ; Isa 40:14 . c. with לְ person 2Chr 35:3 ; Dan 11:33 ; with לְ person & accusative of thing Job 6:24 ; Dan 8:16 . d. בְּ of thing Neh 8:8 , + accusative of person Dan 1:17 . e. double accusative Isa 28:9 ; Psa 119:27 ; Dan 10:14 ; מֵבִין teacher 1Chr 15:22 ; 25:7-8 , 27:32 ; Ezra 8:16 . Hithpa`el Perfect הִתְבּוֺנָ֑ן Isa 1:3 6 t.; Imperfect אֶתְבּוֺנֵן Job 23:15 3 t.; אֶתְבּוֺנָ֑ן 32:12 5 t.; יִתְבּוֺנְנוּ Psa 107:43 2 t.; יִתְבּוֺנָ֑נוּ Isa 14:16 ; 43:18 . 1 shew oneself attentive, consider diligently: — a. absolute Job 11:11 ; 23:15 ; Isa 1:3 ; Jer 2:10 ; 9:16 . b. accusative Job 37:14 ; Psa 107:43 ; 119:95 ; Isa 43:18 ; 52:15 . c. with אֶל 1Kin 3:21 ; Isa 14:16 . d. with עַל Job 31:1 ; Psa 37:10 e. with עד Job 32:12 ; 38:18 . f. with בְּ Job 30:20 ; Jer 23:20 (= 30:24 ). 2 get understanding, understand Job 26:14 ; Psa 119:104 . 3 shew oneself to have understanding Psa 119:100","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 15 22","keyReferences":["1Chr 15 22","1Chr 25 7","1Chr 25 8","1Chr 27 32","1Chr 28 9","1Kgs 3 9","1Kgs 3 11","1Kgs 3 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":171,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 15 22","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מֵבִ֖ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhrmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 25 7","b